# What a close leaves of a reader's note (scenes/about.seed.ts saves the screen as a note): two readers, the first's
# opens wired to the second, which was told no note. The bean rows open in the first, and it is closed: the note
# stays on screen, in the reader the layout says is its heir (the close's answer names it: `heir`, `note`).
bar.open scope=screens query=two-beds
bar.pick n=1
bar.open scope=search query="Bean rows"
bar.pick n=1
tile.close tile=bed
